---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('activecampaign')!;
const b = appBySlug('rejoiner')!;
const path = '/compare/activecampaign-vs-rejoiner';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-rejoiner');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-rejoiner');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should I compare ActiveCampaign with Rejoiner?",
    "answer": "Compare ActiveCampaign when your team will own follow-up automation. Evaluate Rejoiner for platform versus service ownership; demonstrate the required event and operating handoff before choosing."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do these pages establish a recovery winner?",
    "answer": "No merchant trial or incremental lift is established. The workflows and numeric examples are proposed evaluation tools."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I plan timing and incentives?",
    "answer": "Choose timing from checkout behavior and operating constraints. Recheck purchase, inventory, permission and competing queues at dispatch; no universal timing or discount cap is established."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does the numeric example assume?",
    "answer": "A $523 basket at 39% gross margin has $203.97 gross profit at full price. A 14% code removes $73.22 from revenue with unchanged goods cost, before other variable costs."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-16"><div class="container">
<a href="/compare" class="link">← Comparisons</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">{a.name} vs {b.name} for Shopify cart recovery</h1>
<p class="mt-7 text-xl">Platform versus service ownership: compare event coverage, operator responsibilities and recovery cost with your own Shopify checkout.</p>
<TldrBox picks={[{label:"ActiveCampaign",tool:a.name,reason:"An internal owner maintains email recovery and follow-up branches."},{label:"Rejoiner",tool:b.name,reason:"Email platform with optional strategy and creative services."}]} />
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>ActiveCampaign</th><th>Rejoiner</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Evaluation focus</td><td>Cart-triggered email and your team’s follow-up rules</td><td>Email platform with optional strategy and creative services.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Demonstration</td><td>Checkout event, populated cart block and purchase exit</td><td>Platform versus service ownership and purchase suppression</td></tr>
<tr><td>Budget</td><td>Current quote for audience, automation and implementation</td><td>Current quote including required channels and service scope</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Separate software access from managed work</h2>
<p>Rejoiner offers a platform and optional professional services. Its pricing page distinguishes strategy guidance from a creative package covering planning, content, design and deployment. A software subscription does not automatically buy that work. ActiveCampaign is a candidate when an internal team wants to maintain recovery automation; compare Rejoiner when outsourcing some of that work addresses an actual staffing gap.</p>
<h2>Use a concrete creative brief</h2>
<p>For a gift basket abandoned at the message field, ask the operator to verify that the return link preserves the gift choices. For a high-value financing interruption, require copy that answers payment questions without promising approval. Give both operators the same products, offer rules, exclusions and approval deadline. Evaluate whether each can explain the event and safely release the flow; this is a proposed exercise, not a measured performance contest.</p>
<h2>Specify approvals and access</h2>
<p>Before commissioning a managed flow, name the person who approves incentives and the person who can pause sends. Request editable templates, workflow documentation, reporting access and a handover procedure. Ask what happens to pending campaigns if creative approval is late or the service engagement ends. Internal teams still need time for catalog changes, customer questions and review of supplier work.</p>
<h2>Compare the complete operating cost</h2>
<p>Quote platform access, audience size, SMS where required, service scope, implementation and internal review time separately. A managed engagement can reduce execution work while adding approval and handoff dependencies. No retainer saving, recovery benchmark or third-party winner is established here. Test the required email workflow first; include an SMS branch only after its sender, market coverage and permissions are demonstrated.</p>
<h2>Check the ActiveCampaign event before designing branches</h2>
<p><a href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/360001045964-Abandoned-cart-overview">ActiveCampaign’s cart documentation</a> describes email automation and a cart content block. For Shopify it documents a checkout-stage requirement for data sync. A product-page visitor or anonymous cart is not automatically eligible. Record the integration wait and workflow delay separately, then inspect the actual event payload and destination.</p>
<h2>Retain margin math without implying results</h2>
<p>Illustrative basket: $523 at 39% gross margin has $319.03 goods cost and $203.97 full-price gross profit. A 14% code leaves $449.78 revenue and $130.75 gross profit, a $73.22 reduction. Goods cost is unchanged. Subtract fulfillment, payment, message and return costs before calling the remainder contribution. This does not show an incremental recovery by either product.</p>
<h2>Cut over and measure deliberately</h2>
<p>Inventory Shopify and provider recovery flows, pause competing queues and assign one owner per event and channel. Reconcile opt-outs and purchases before enabling the replacement. Compare deduplicated contribution per eligible shopper over the same window. If a randomized no-message group is feasible, choose allocation and duration from traffic, conversion delay and the effect you need to detect. Keep a rollback owner for broken links or failed purchase exits.</p>
<p>Product scope checked November 25, 2026: <a href="https://www.rejoiner.com/pricing">Rejoiner primary documentation</a>. Select the setup whose demonstrated workflow and staffing model fit your store; no ratings or universal winner are supplied.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title={`${a.name} vs ${b.name} FAQ`} />
</div></section></BaseLayout>
